'''''Erica scoparia''''', the '''green heather'''<ref>{{cite web |title=Erica scoparia (green heather) |url=https://www.cabi.org/isc/datasheet/20539 |publisher=[[Invasive Species Compendium]] |access-date=14 February 2021}}</ref> or '''common besom heath''',<ref>{{Cite web |title=Common Besom Heath (Erica scoparia) |url=https://www.inaturalist.org/taxa/771657-Erica-scoparia |access-date=2023-11-03 |website=iNaturalist |language=en}}</ref> is a shrubby European species of [[heath]] in the [[flowering plant]] family [[Ericaceae]].

== Description ==
''Erica scoparia'' is a [[perennial plant|perennial]] [[evergreen]] [[shrub]] with small yellowish white to red-brown bell-shaped drooping [[flower]]s borne in clusters at the ends of its shoots.<ref>[http://www.florealpes.com/fiche_ericascoaria.php FloreAlpes: Erica scoparia]</ref>

== Distribution and habitat ==
It is native to the western [[Mediterranean Basin]] in the [[Iberian Peninsula]] ([[Spain]] and [[Portugal]]), Northwest Africa ([[Morocco]], [[Algeria]] and [[Tunisia]]), Southern [[France]], [[Italy]], [[Balearic Islands]], [[Sardinia]] and [[Corsica]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Erica scoparia L. |url=https://www.catalogueoflife.org/data/taxon/6GLC3 |access-date=12 August 2022 |publisher=[[Catalogue of Life]]}}</ref>

It is found in a range of Mediterranean habitats, including semi-arid locations. Its distribution seems to largely depend on water availability (being considered [[Hygrophyte|hygrophytic]]) and dissolved [[aluminum]] in the soil. It is quite consistent under varied levels [[Shade tolerance|of shade]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Ojeda |first=Fernando |last2=Arroyo |first2=Juan |last3=Marañón |first3=Teodoro |date=2000 |title=Ecological Distribution of Four Co-Occurring Mediterranean Heath Species |url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/3682877 |journal=Ecography |volume=23 |issue=1 |pages=148–159 |issn=0906-7590}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Antunes |first=Cristina |last2=Díaz Barradas |first2=Mari Cruz |last3=Zunzunegui |first3=Maria |last4=Vieira |first4=Simone |last5=Pereira |first5=Ângela |last6=Anjos |first6=Andreia |last7=Correia |first7=Otília |last8=Pereira |first8=Maria João |last9=Máguas |first9=Cristina |date=23 March 2018 |editor-last=Llorens |editor-first=Laura |title=Contrasting plant water‐use responses to groundwater depth in coastal dune ecosystems |url=https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/1365-2435.13110 |journal=Functional Ecology |language=en |volume=32 |issue=8 |pages=1931–1943 |doi=10.1111/1365-2435.13110 |issn=0269-8463 |doi-access=free|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

